================================================================================
py4DSTEM (conventions)
================================================================================

The lattice convention of those applications (a along x, b in the xy plane; reciprocal vectors
without 2 pi; structure factors in A) follows py4DSTEM's Crystal class
(py4DSTEM/process/diffraction/crystal.py). The Lobato & Van Dyck electron
scattering table of DiffractoScattering is py4DSTEM's (commit f050d207,
scattering_factors.txt, sha256 be845d1d..., fetched by
tools/pins/structure-factors/fetch-table.sh into the gitignored References/ and pinned bit for
bit), and the ring fit's models follow py4DSTEM's fit_ellipse_1D and
fit_ellipse_amorphous_ring (process/calibration/ellipse.py) through
mac4DSTEM's port.

    py4DSTEM - https://github.com/py4dstem/py4DSTEM
    Copyright (C) The py4DSTEM developers
    Licensed under the GNU General Public License v3.0

================================================================================
pymatgen (used as a reference for checking; no code copied)
================================================================================

Cells, expanded CIF sites, symmetry operations (spglib behind pymatgen),
d-spacings and the reflections within a sphere are checked against pymatgen
2026.9.24 / pymatgen-core 2026.10.16 by tools/pins/cells/pins.py, whose output
is the committed fixture pymatgen-cells-pins.json. The Laue orbit and the absence rule are
computed from pymatgen's operations in NumPy.

