================================================================================
Thronsen et al. (phase mapping)
================================================================================

The vector-matching method of DiffractoOrientation (PhaseReferenceLibrary.swift, PhaseVectorMatching.swift and the
PhaseVectorMatcher+*.swift and PhaseVectorTypes.swift files split from it), including the decision rule of `.knownVariants` (in
PhaseVectorMatcher+Classify.swift) and its two constants (direct-matrix count 1, residual cutoff 0.07 inverse angstrom), follow:

    E. Thronsen, J. Hjelen, R. Holmestad et al., "Studying GPB zones and precipitates in Al-Cu-Li with scanning precession
    electron diffraction", Ultramicroscopy 255 (2024) 113861, licensed CC BY 4.0
    (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Changes: re-implemented in Swift from the published description.

No code was copied from the authors' notebook; their repository carries no licence.

================================================================================
Orientation symmetry and IPF keys
================================================================================

NativeIPFKeys.swift ports the native direction folds, samplers and colour keys
from mac4DSTEM c809679c, mac4DSTEM/Core/Analysis/OrientationResult.swift
(GPL-3.0). The application's orientation-map container is not included.
Py4DSTEMIPFKey.swift reimplements the full-mask beam colour part of py4DSTEM
f050d207851f8accd3aa550365baaf1f38230428, crystal_viz.py
plot_orientation_maps (GPL-3.0); its automatic sector bases are generated by
calling that version's orientation_plan. pymatgen PointGroup (2026.9.24 /
core 2026.10.16, MIT) is an oracle for all eleven proper rotation tables;
SciPy Rotation is an oracle for the minimum-angle representative. No orix or
MTEX code is copied into the library. tools/pins/orientation-symmetry/pins.py records
provenance.

